  "statement": "```\nDataFrame students\n+-------------+--------+\n| Column Name | Type   |\n+-------------+--------+\n| student_id  | int    |\n| name        | object |\n| age         | int    |\n+-------------+--------+\n```\n\nWrite a solution to select the name and age of the student with `student_id = 101`.\n\nThe result format is in the following example.\n\n```\nExample 1:\nInput:\n+------------+---------+-----+\n| student_id | name    | age |\n+------------+---------+-----+\n| 101        | Ulysses | 13  |\n| 53         | William | 10  |\n| 128        | Henry   | 6   |\n| 3          | Henry   | 11  |\n+------------+---------+-----+\nOutput:\n+---------+-----+\n| name    | age | \n+---------+-----+\n| Ulysses | 13  |\n+---------+-----+\nExplanation:\nStudent Ulysses has student_id = 101, we select the name and age.\n```",
  "constraints": [],
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "+------------+---------+-----+\n| student_id | name    | age |\n+------------+---------+-----+\n| 101        | Ulysses | 13  |\n| 53         | William | 10  |\n| 128        | Henry   | 6   |\n| 3          | Henry   | 11  |\n+------------+---------+-----+",
      "output": "+---------+-----+\n| name    | age | \n+---------+-----+\n| Ulysses | 13  |\n+---------+-----+",
      "explanation": "Student Ulysses has student_id = 101, we select the name and age."
    }
  ],
  "starterCode": {
    "pythondata": "import pandas as pd\n\ndef selectData(students: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    "
  },
